mapping "e125.1" source="e125" target="SNOMED_CT:224900001" relationship=related_to effect=omitted quality=40 {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e125 SNOMED CT 224900001 = ICF environmental factor: products and technology for
        communication. Target (Device/Physical Object, standard_concept=S; sv synonym). This is the only
        standard SNOMED CT concept with direct semantic overlap to e125. Relationship is, not identity: the
        ICF code is an ENVIRONMENTAL FACTOR (contextual product/technology), whereas the SNOMED CT concept
        denotes the physical device object itself. A contextual/source-of-environment code mapped to the
        referenced object is a loose link, capped at (weak). Not exact/broader/narrower because source
        and target are different semantic kinds (context vs object).
        """
}
mapping "e1250.1" source="e1250" target="SNOMED_CT:224900001" relationship=related_to effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e1250 SNOMED CT 224900001 = ICF environmental factor: general (non-adapted) communication
        products/technology. Target (standard device; sv). General communication products are loosely
        associated with communication aids but the source is a contextual environmental factor, the
        target is a device object; link at. The qualifier slightly weakens the fit versus e125 but the
        same standard concept remains the only defensible target.
        """
}
mapping "e1251.1" source="e1251" target="SNOMED_CT:705438004" relationship=related_to effect=omitted quality=40 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e1251 SNOMED CT 705438004 = ICF environmental factor: assistive (adapted) communication
        products/technology. Target (standard_concept=S). This is the assistive-communication device
        concept and the closest standard match for the meaning. Relationship is : the ICF code is a
        contextual environmental factor, the SNOMED CT concept is the physical device object; loose link
        capped at. Not exact because of the context-vs-object semantic gap.
        """
}
